.nh
.TH "PB-POLICY-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-policy-set - Validate and save a workspace policy file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb policy set <file|-> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Check a policy file locally, validate it on the server against the saved
policy, print any errors, test results and the access each change grants or
removes, then save it. A save that changes anyone's access asks for
confirmation; --yes confirms the printed changes without asking. --dry-run
stops after validation. Use - to read the file from standard input.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	validate and print the changes without saving

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--message\fP=""
	describe the change in the version history

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	confirm the printed access changes without asking


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb policy set policy.hujson
  pb policy set policy.hujson --dry-run
  pb policy get | pb policy set - --yes --message "tidy"
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-policy(1)\fP
